<title>SYRIA: Syria bans tobacco advertising.</title>
<headline>Syria bans tobacco advertising.</headline>
<dateline>DAMASCUS 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Hafez al-Assad has banned tobacco advertising in Syria, officials said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>They said Assad issued a legislative decree setting 4-12 months in jail and a fine of 25,000-100,000 Syrian pounds ($500-$2,000) as punishment for violators.</p>
<p>The ban covers advertisements for all types of tobacco on media and other means of publicity, the officials said.</p>
</text>
